@1 = ~Absent-minded artist~
@2 = ~A Half-elven artist from Bridge District cannot focus due to constant noises and asked us to find a potion of mind focusing for him so he can finish his drawing.~
@3 = ~We brought Irving a Potion of Mind Focusing. He can finally concentrate on his drawings, and he gave us one of his earlier sketches as thanks.~

// CotSC localisation batch 4: player-visible text extracted; original entries unchanged.
@4 = ~Is anyone going to finally do something about these murders? Anyone at all?~
@5 = ~What can you tell us about it?~
@6 = ~I'm afraid I cannot help you.~
@7 = ~Homeless people like me are skinned alive. Horrid. Of all ways to die I do not wish to die like this. You should ask around. Some homeless people around here might be able to tell you more. I keep to myself really and I spent my nights in hiding majority of time.~
@8 = ~(sigh) Courage is so underrated nowadays.~
@9 = ~No fish. Fish mine. You go buy fish somewhere else.~
@10 = ~I cannot hear my own thoughts. Everyone stomping around, mumbling, yelling, crying, screaming, barking, I have enough! All I want is to be able to concentrate on my drawings.~
@11 = ~What are you drawing?~
@12 = ~Ehm... I'll stomp around somewhere else. Bye.~
@13 = ~The sea. I am an artist. Well, I like to call myself an artist as this is my passion but I assure you my skills develop with each drawing. Problem is that I lose focus every couple seconds due to constant disruptions of the environment. I understand the tough times we live in but I am not asking for much when I say I want some peace and quiet. If you could do me a favour and bring me a potion of mind focusing, I'd give you one of my drawings.~
@14 = ~I can't finish that drawing. My inspirations keep getting out of my head!~
@15 = ~I have a potion of mind focusing for you. Here.~
@16 = ~I'll be back when I find a potion for you.~
@17 = ~You do? Oh, this is fantastic. Phenomenal. Now, I'll be able to finish the drawing. As I promised, here you go. My previous drawing. I do have talent, don't you think?~
@18 = ~Now I'll finally be able to finish the drawing.~
@19 = ~Woah. I don't have any gold. I swear.~
@20 = ~I'm not here to steal from you.~
@21 = ~Ehm... gold? Oh, yeah. I know you have gold. Better give it to me. Now!~
@22 = ~Right. I... I thought you might... you just look like a common thief. No offence, it's just typical in these areas. I'll be going now.~
@23 = ~Okay! Okay! Here. That is all I have, I swear!~
@24 = ~Please, I don't want no trouble.~
@25 = ~No matter who you are, I am NOT interested! How many times do I have to blow people off because they want to find out if they can beat me. I may be stronger than y'all but that doesn't mean I am going to fight you. Now, piss off!~
@26 = ~Mind your own business, dwarf or else I...~
@27 = ~You're a dead man!~
@28 = ~I despise this city so much but you know what they say. Beggars can't be choosers. I lived most in my life in the wilderness as a bandit until I came across a random adventurer who turned my life around. Do I regret becoming a better person? YES! I don't get to pillage, and therefore I don't get to make money. I'm a standard fisherman now. What a joke.~
@29 = ~Whatever you say, preacher. I will abstain from putting you in your place.~
@30 = ~Excuse me. Are you... the hero of Baldur's Gate?~
@31 = ~Some call me that. Why?~
@32 = ~My name is Alina. I lived across the street from Elfsong tavern. I just want to say, I am grateful for all you've done. Despite of... what you are. I am in your debt. Your heritage or the fact that you were responsible for Skie's murder...~
@33 = ~... what I meant to say is, I don't believe these allegations. You saved the city from the war. I am grateful.~
@34 = ~It's fine. Really.~
@35 = ~I'll leave you be now. Stay safe.~
@36 = ~Stay out of trouble.~
@37 = ~Hic... and then I say, HIC... size don't matter! Because I am rising to the occasion! He, he...~
@38 = ~It isn't the truth. <CHARNAME> is not responsible for her death. This is a misunderstanding.~
@39 = ~A goblin fisherman? That's a rare sight indeed.~
@40 = ~What 'ave we got 'ere? A backpedalin' coward hidin' away, pretendin' to be stronger than me?! Feh!~
@41 = ~Ye're gon' what?! Feed me to the fishies?! Step up, ye spineless milksop, and show me what ye got! Me axe is thirstin' for yer blood!~
@42 = ~You regret leaving the life of a murderous clotpole? Your presence in this city is a stain on its reputation.~
@43 = ~(sigh) If anyone still wonders if alcohol is poison, here's your answer.~
